{"ts": 0.129513, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m4.3 — redirection and globs\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA pipe sends output to \u001b[36manother program\u001b[0m. A redirect sends it\r\nto \u001b[36ma file\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92m>\u001b[0m    write to a file (\u001b[91moverwrites\u001b[0m if it exists)\r\n  \u001b[92m>>\u001b[0m   append to a file (creates if missing)\r\n  \u001b[92m<\u001b[0m    read a file \u001b[36minto\u001b[0m a command\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n  \u001b[92mecho first > greeting.txt\u001b[0m        \u001b[90m# overwrite\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho second >> greeting.txt\u001b[0m      \u001b[90m# append\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcat greeting.txt\u001b[0m                 \u001b[90m# two lines\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -w < poem.txt\u001b[0m                 \u001b[90m# count words read from poem.txt\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nCombine with pipes:\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | sort > programs.txt\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l programs.txt\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mGlobs\u001b[0m match many filenames at once. The shell expands them\r\n\u001b[36mbefore\u001b[0m the command sees them.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mls *.txt\u001b[0m              \u001b[90m# every .txt file in this folder\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l *.txt\u001b[0m           \u001b[90m# count lines in each .txt file\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcat *.txt\u001b[0m             \u001b[90m# print them a", "len": 1024}
{"ts": 0.129604, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "ll back-to-back\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mPredict before you act.\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mrm *\u001b[0m removes everything\r\nin the current folder. \u001b[92mrm *.tmp\u001b[0m removes only .tmp files.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to take Stage 4's gate.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 218}
